#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# random_normal

#% text
# `random_normal()` gives a machine real from the standard normal distribution; `random_normal(mu, sigma)` from the normal distribution with mean `mu` and standard deviation `sigma`.
# `random_normal(mu, sigma, n)` gives a list of `n` of them; `[n1, n2, ...]` gives an array.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The draws come from the session generator; `seed(k)` makes them reproducible.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
seed(1); random_normal()
#% output
#= -0.8289777865469348

#% cell
seed(1); random_normal(10, 2, 5)
#% output
#= [8.342044426906131, 7.961814596840059, 13.075859784335181, 10.867251516087766, 10.820685436010395]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The sample mean and standard deviation approach the parameters:

#% cell
seed(2); xs = random_normal(5, 3, 100000); [mean(xs), std_dev(xs)]
#% output
#= [5.00234598462906, 3.012576142811012]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `random_real`, `random_variate`, `normal_distribution`, `seed`
